msgstr "Proprietary Kode"

#: src/gs-safety-context-dialog.c:349
msgid ""
"The source code is not public, so it cannot be independently audited and "
"might be unsafe"
msgstr ""
"Die bronkode is nie publiek nie, dus kan dit nie onafhanklik geoudit word en "
"mag dalk onveilig"

#. Translators: This refers to permissions (for example, from flatpak) which an app requests from the user.
#: src/gs-safety-context-dialog.c:352
msgid "Auditable Code"
msgstr "Ouditeerbare Kode"

#: src/gs-safety-context-dialog.c:353
msgid ""
"The source code is public and can be independently audited, which makes the "
"app more likely to be safe"
msgstr ""
"Die bronkode is publiek en kan wees onafhanklik geoudit, watter maak die "
"toepassing meer geneig om veilig"

#. Translators: This indicates an app was written and released by a developer who has been verified.
#. * It’s used in a context tile, so should be short.
#: src/gs-safety-context-dialog.c:361
msgid "App developer is verified"
msgstr "App ontwikkelaar is geverifieer"

#: src/gs-safety-context-dialog.c:362
msgid ""
"The developer of this app has been verified to be who they say they are"
msgstr ""
"Die ontwikkelaar van hierdie app het wees geverifieer om wie hulle sê hulle "
"is"

